        "original_id": "801cc9d5-e44f-5be6-b881-9a5bbee70f57",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ozzy Osbourne, Curt Smith, Roland Orzabal\n- Organizations: Black Sabbath, Tears for Fears\n- Works: Change, Mothers Talk, solo albums, studio albums\n- Roles: singer, songwriter, actor, bassist, solo artist\n\nFacts:\n- Ozzy Osbourne was born on 3 December 1948 and is an English singer, songwriter, and actor.\n- Black Sabbath fired Ozzy Osbourne in 1979.\n- Ozzy Osbourne then had a successful solo career and released 11 studio albums, with his first seven studio albums receiving multi-platinum certifications in the United States.\n- \"Mothers Talk\" is a 1984 song by the British band Tears for Fears.\n- \"Change\" was written by Roland Orzabal, sung by Tears for Fears bassist Curt Smith, and released as the band's fourth single.\n- Curt Smith has released four solo albums as a solo artist.",
